@tylerszabo and @Heisenberg2980 I have added some major improvements to the statistics integration over the last couple of days. Please wait for the 2021.12 Home Assistant release and give it another try.

@Heisenberg2980 the behavior might be correct. Count represents the number of sensor readings within the defined timespan. Did you consider that there are always exactly 20 readings?

@tylerszabo your count should be shown as a graph with 2021.12. Please verify and close the issue if everything is fine.

@Heisenberg2980 just realized that your issue is unrelated to the one by @tylerszabo and a user config error. Generally it's advised to discuss these kinds of issues in the Home Assistant community forum.

Please see: https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/statistics/#sampling_size

If you do not set `sampling_size` and/or `max_age` the count of measurements will be limited by the default of `sampling size`, which is 20 :) Not sure what you are trying to accomplish but you need to adapt your sensor config.

@tylerszabo thanks for the feedback, I can see that!

Please check whether my latest changes (to be released with 2021.12) do solve these clarity issues.

https://deploy-preview-20543--home-assistant-docs.netlify.app/integrations/statistics/

Thanks for linking your previous issue. I agree with your critique. Cleaning up with the whole sampling_size and/or max_age mess is on my todo list. The current way these are handled make no sense to me. Why is there an implicit sampling_size of 20? Why no default max_age?

Please check the preview above and let me know what you would like to see additionally.

@Heisenberg2980 same goes for you. Any hints which part of the current documentation article threw you off and where the new version could still be better?
